; setline_binary_sample_out_of_domain: a binary sample holds {0, 1} and
; nothing else.
;
; Until QUI-1168 both implementations accepted any i64 here and GETLINE read
; it back, so a binary sample could hold 2 and a solver could be handed an
; assignment that is not an assignment. The domain is a property of the
; sample's allocator, so the check needs no operand and no annotation: BSMX
; declared it.
;
; 2 is one past the top rather than a wild value, which pins the bound
; itself. Writing 1 into the same slot is correct and is what
; sample_linear_ops covers.

PUSH 4
BSMX r0          ; binary sample, domain {0, 1}

PUSH 1
PUSH 2           ; one past the top of the domain
SETLINE r0
HALT
